sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor HR as HR manager
    participant UI as React app
    participant API as API (Express)
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    Note over HR,DB: Employee directory
    HR->>UI: Search, filter, sort, or include inactive
    UI->>API: GET /api/employees?search=&department=&sort=-annualTotal&page=1&currency=USD
    API->>API: Apply the user's country scope to the query
    API->>DB: One query on employees and current pay totals, with LIMIT/OFFSET and a total count
    API-->>UI: One page of rows, amounts in USD or local currency
    UI-->>HR: Table shows the page, cached by TanStack Query

    Note over HR,DB: Pay change
    HR->>UI: Change components, effective date and reason
    UI->>API: POST /api/employees/:id/pay-changes
    API->>DB: In one transaction, close the changed pay items and add the new ones
    API-->>UI: 201, then the UI refreshes the employee, list and dashboard

    Note over HR,DB: Dashboard
    HR->>UI: Open the dashboard, USD toggle on or off
    UI->>API: GET /api/insights/pay-range-by-country, by-job-title, cost-by-department, outliers
    API->>DB: GROUP BY queries: count, min, max, avg, percentile_cont, within the user's scope
    API->>DB: Latest exchange rates when amounts are shown in USD
    API-->>UI: Statistics and the date of the rates used
    UI-->>HR: Charts and tables
